On 3/30/18 at 7:35 PM, pgut001@cs.auckland.ac.nz (Peter Gutmann) wrote:

>As you mention, debugging TLS is unnecessarily painful if there's a proble=
m,
>you typically just get a handshake-failed alert which is essentially no
>information at all.  Having a debug-mode capability to send back a long-fo=
rm
>error message would be extremely useful, maybe an extension to say "send b=
ack
>a long-form alert with more than just 'BOOLEAN succeeded =3D FALSE' in it"=
.

We have always avoided the long form error messages in TLS=20
because they can be of great help to attackers as well as=20
debuggers. I think this objection is much weaker if we write the=20
long form error messages into a log that is kept with other=20
server logs.

Cheers - Bill

